# uSD card prep — one card per drone — 2026-09-14
#
# Both drones need their OWN uSD card, formatted FAT32, with
# flying_drone_stack/tools/usd_thesis_config.txt copied to the card root AS config.txt
# (exact filename, not the original name -- the firmware only reads "config.txt").
# Do this once per card; cards then just live in each drone permanently.

# ── 1. Find the card's device node (do this AFTER inserting ONE card at a time --
#      makes it unambiguous which device just appeared) ─────────────────────────────────
lsblk
# Look for a new device (e.g. /dev/sdb1 or /dev/mmcblk0p1) that wasn't there before.
# DOUBLE CHECK this is the SD card and not a system disk before the next steps --
# mkfs on the wrong device destroys data with no warning.

# ── 2. Format FAT32 (replace sdX1 with the real device from step 1) ─────────────────────
sudo umount /dev/sdX1 2>/dev/null   # unmount first if auto-mounted
sudo mkfs.vfat -F 32 -n THESIS /dev/sdX1

# ── 3. Mount, copy config, unmount cleanly ───────────────────────────────────────────────
mkdir -p /tmp/sdcard_mount
sudo mount /dev/sdX1 /tmp/sdcard_mount
cp /home/flyingrobots/georg/flying_robot_course/flying_drone_stack/tools/usd_thesis_config.txt \
   /tmp/sdcard_mount/config.txt
sync
sudo umount /tmp/sdcard_mount

# ── 4. Repeat steps 1-3 for the SECOND card (cf_second's) ────────────────────────────────
# Insert the second card, run `lsblk` again to find its (likely different) device node,
# then repeat the format + copy for it too. Two separate physical cards, same config.txt
# content on both -- the config just says WHAT to log, not which drone it's on.

# ── 5. Insert each card into its drone, power on, confirm detection ─────────────────────
# cf231_active is on the DEV machine's check_usd_deck.py (URI radio://0/80/2M/E7E7E7E7E7) --
# copy that script's URI or just edit it in place for cf_second's URI
# (radio://0/80/2M/E7E7E7E7E9) to check that one too. Run from terminal 2 (sourced env):
python3 /home/flyingrobots/georg/flying_robot_course/flying_drone_stack/tools/check_usd_deck.py
# Expect: "usd param group found: [...]" and "usd.logging current value = ..." with no
# MISSING lines. If MISSING, the deck itself isn't seated/detected -- reseat it, don't
# just re-copy the config file.

# ── After both cards are prepped and confirmed detected ──────────────────────────────────
# Re-fly A8 (same command as before) -- run_formation.py already turns usd.logging on/off
# automatically around the scenario (`allcfs.setParam('usd.logging', 1/0)`), no extra flag
# needed. After landing, pull each card's binary log file off (card root, likely named by
# timestamp or index depending on firmware log-writer naming) and I'll write the
# uSD-vs-radio sync comparison once we have both files -- tools/merge_usd_logs.py and
# tools/decode_usd_log.py already exist for this, just never run on real 2-drone data yet.
